{title: My Faith Looks Up to Thee}
{artist: Ray Palmer & Lowell Mason}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}

Verse 1
[D]My faith looks [G]up to [D]thee, thou [G]Lamb of [D]Calva[A]ry, [D]Savior di[A]vine:
[D]now hear me [G]while I [D]pray, [G]take all my [D]guilt a[A]way,
[D]O let me [A]from this [Bm]day [G]be [D]wholly [A]thine.

Verse 2
[D]May Thy rich [G]grace impart [D]Strength to my [G]fainting heart, [D]my [D]zeal inspire!
[D]As Thou hast [G]died for [D]me, [G]O may my [D]love to
[D]Thee, Pure warm, [A]and changeless [Bm]be, [G]a [D]living [A]fire!

Verse 3
[D]While life's dark [G]maze I [D]tread, And [G]griefs around [D]me [D]spread, be
[D]Thou my Guide; [G]Bid darkness [D]turn [G]to day, wipe [D]sorrow's tears
[D]away, Nor let [A]me ever [Bm]stray [G]from [D]Thee [A]aside.

Verse 4
[D]When ends life's [G]transient dream, [D]When death's [G]cold sullen [D]stream [D]over me
[D]roll; Blest Savior, [G]then in [G]love, fear and [D]distrust remove;
[D]O bear me [A]safe [Bm]above, [G]a [D]ransomed [A]soul!
